Why this licence, and how to change it. All-rights-reserved is the only
one-way-reversible choice: it can become MIT (or anything else) at any moment,
whereas code once published under MIT stays MIT for those copies forever. It
costs nothing, forecloses nothing, and removes the ambiguity a recipient of a
build would otherwise face. If the owner later wants portfolio visibility or
reuse, replacing this file with an OSI licence is a one-commit decision.
